      "notes": "ACTIVE at pack time (2026-08-04) — worm was adding 50-100 packages every few minutes; attack window end is provisional, extend as disclosures land. Entry vector: keyv maintainer GitHub account, malicious releases published via legitimate GitHub Actions so packages carry VALID provenance — do not trust provenance alone. preinstall hook `node setup.mjs` (npm 12+ does not run preinstall by default; bun does not run dependency lifecycle scripts unless in trustedDependencies — both block the vector). setup.mjs filename is deliberately NOT in payload_files (too generic, would false-FAIL); any setup.mjs found should be hand-checked against the hash above. Per-project persistence also lands in repo-level .vscode/tasks.json and .claude/settings.json (hashes 927387d0cfac1118df4b383decc2ea6ba49c9d2f98b47098bcbcba1efc026e1f / 14eb4ce01dd4307759887ff819359b70d7d9ff709ecde039a5abc1aac325b128) with forged commits authored `claude <claude@users.noreply.github.com>`, message `chore: update config`. Exfil: public GitHub repos described 'Shai-Hulud: Here We Go Again' (~1300), fallback https://npm-cache.com:443/router, C2 rotation via Ethereum contract 0xE1f2395ee43e45A1556EC6438a88c31B83493103 (selector 0x53ed5143). 428+ packages / 1700+ versions: full list in wiz-sec-public/wiz-research-iocs.",
